WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:03.639
Let's go next to our caller from the three
47 area code.

00:00:03.639 --> 00:00:05.700
Who's calling today from three four seven.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:08.210
Oh, it was the snake.

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:09.210
Yes it is.

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:10.210
Who's this?

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:11.210
Okay,

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:13.099
this is Alex from Brooklyn, New York.

00:00:13.099 --> 00:00:15.219
Hey Alex, what's up?

00:00:15.219 --> 00:00:17.440
So I had two things on my mind.

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:19.210
One is sort of my opinion.

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:21.860
One I wanted to ask for yours.

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:24.850
And they're both, uh, an opinion [inaudible]

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:29.300
uh, they're both related to impeachment rather
than Iran.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:30.510
Sure.

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:31.730
[inaudible]

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:34.300
so the first thing I wanted to talk about

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:43.100
was this like idea from Democrats sort of
like this, you know, examination of this impeachment

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:50.550
that um, you know, as this thing will progress
and maybe afterwards, no Americans will kind

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:55.570
of look back on this and think, Oh my goodness,
how could we support Trump?

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:56.680
Like what is going on?

00:00:56.680 --> 00:01:08.400
Like we fell to this ideology and, um, just
sort of, um, fear-mongering that led us to

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:15.040
vote for Trump when in reality, in my opinion,
we're going to have something more along the

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:22.130
lines of how people look at the civil war
in the sense of that there's still a population

00:01:22.130 --> 00:01:28.020
in this country that still thinks that the
civil war was, you know, Northern digression

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:33.299
or it's about, you know, disruption of state
rights and whatnot.

00:01:33.299 --> 00:01:34.299
That's interesting.

00:01:34.299 --> 00:01:38.720
So if I understand correctly, what you're
saying is no matter what happens during the

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:44.600
Trump administration with Iran or with anything
else, eventually there will be people who

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:47.729
will see Trump as this great hero.

00:01:47.729 --> 00:01:52.950
Much like you still have people who see the
civil war as being about States' rights rather

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:54.510
than about slavery or whatever.

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:57.330
Like there will always be a contingent that
sees it that way.

00:01:57.330 --> 00:01:58.330
Yes.

00:01:58.330 --> 00:02:05.299
When I see like kids that Trump rallies, you
know, sharing them on, I feel like many years

00:02:05.299 --> 00:02:09.239
from now they'll tell their kids Trump with
the greatest president ever.

00:02:09.239 --> 00:02:15.719
Uh, whether it's, you know, ends in 10 months
or four and a half years, but [inaudible]

00:02:15.719 --> 00:02:17.510
I don't think it wrong.

00:02:17.510 --> 00:02:21.790
I think maybe you're overstating the importance
that Trump is going to have historically.

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:23.209
I mean, I hope so.

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:28.079
I hope that historically Trump will be seen
as, as an aberration, but that people won't

00:02:28.079 --> 00:02:32.049
talk about him that much one way or the other
much the same way that a lot of presidents

00:02:32.049 --> 00:02:34.609
aren't really discussed very much today.

00:02:34.609 --> 00:02:38.620
But the more erratic has behavior of course
the more likely that he does remain a topic

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:39.620
of conversation.

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:40.799
But it's an interesting point of view for
sure.

00:02:40.799 --> 00:02:44.720
The idea that there's always going to be at
the same time though, you know, if you think

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:50.219
back to like William Howard Taft, is there
a contingent that goes around idolizing Taft

00:02:50.219 --> 00:02:51.219
today?

00:02:51.219 --> 00:02:54.629
He just kind of become, not, not, not a big
factor.

00:02:54.629 --> 00:02:59.529
Maybe Trump would be the same, although certainly
he, he would, uh, ideally be seen as an aberration

00:02:59.529 --> 00:03:02.689
no matter how long it goes.

00:03:02.689 --> 00:03:04.069
I hope as well.

00:03:04.069 --> 00:03:05.069
Yeah.

00:03:05.069 --> 00:03:08.999
And the second point that I want to bring
up actually does relate to the impeachment

00:03:08.999 --> 00:03:11.579
trials, but it also has something to do with
Iran.

00:03:11.579 --> 00:03:19.110
So I was watching one of your videos, um,
about Techron Carlson talking about how, you

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:23.830
know, we shouldn't be in this war with Iran,
like so on and so forth.

00:03:23.830 --> 00:03:29.719
And he mentioned John Bolton as a non genius
and you know, to a certain point, I agree

00:03:29.719 --> 00:03:31.079
with them on that.

00:03:31.079 --> 00:03:32.079
Yeah.

00:03:32.079 --> 00:03:38.870
But in his commentary, he sort of, you know,
dismisses John Bolton and I was wondering

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:45.749
if you think he might be playing this sort
of like side role of dismissing John Bolton

00:03:45.749 --> 00:03:50.909
because in the case that he does somehow end
up testifying in the Senate, although with

00:03:50.909 --> 00:03:51.909
[inaudible]

00:03:51.909 --> 00:03:52.909
yeah,

00:03:52.909 --> 00:03:58.629
we can play off as you know, this guy, he's
a warmonger and you know, even though he,

00:03:58.629 --> 00:04:04.599
I don't believe he had anything to, he had
anything to do with Iran, he on the other

00:04:04.599 --> 00:04:11.809
hand could be dismissed as just another warmonger
and his testimony is worth little to nothing.

00:04:11.809 --> 00:04:16.320
I don't think that that's Tucker's motivation,
if anything, uh, it, it's just that Tucker

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:21.200
has always had disagreements with John Bolton
because John volt Bolton is very interventionist

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:24.010
and Tucker Carlson has an anti interventionist
streak.

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:26.590
I don't think it's nearly as calculated as,
as you're suggesting.

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:28.410
Uh, Alex, thank you so much.

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:29.410
Great to hear from you.

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:32.080
I do have to move on to other callers and
I hope to hear from you again.

